# Supabase — public client configuration.
#
# Both values below are public by design: they are compiled into the browser
# bundle on every build, so they are already visible to anyone who loads the
# site. What actually protects your data is Row Level Security on each table
# (see docs/SUPABASE.md) — not the secrecy of this key.
#
# Environment variables set in the hosting platform (Vercel: Project Settings →
# Environment Variables) override this file, which is the better home for them
# if you would rather they not live in the repository.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here. It bypasses RLS and this file is
# committed.

# This is also the hostname Google shows on its sign-in sheet ("to continue to
# …"). To put your own name there instead, follow docs/AUTH-DOMAIN.md and change
# this one value to https://auth.quickstark.tech — nothing in the code hardcodes
# the Supabase host, so that is the whole change.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://esuatccbicekcohzgcvd.supabase.co
